load @term/seed/algebra/root-system
  find root-system

# The rotation algebra of eight-dimensional space, the algebra called D four, the home of triality. It is forced from the octonions two ways at once. From above, it is the rotation structure of the dimension where the reversible tower tops out. From below, it is the unique rank where the vector and the half-spinor have the same size, eight against two cubed, the one-substance demand. Its rank is four, the dimension of spacetime, one ordered direction and three unordered. Its root system is the 24-cell, and its threefold symmetry, triality, cycles its three eight-dimensional pieces and lives nowhere else.
form d4
  link roots, like root-system

# D4, proof-checked by `seed test`.

# The one-substance demand: the half-spinor and the vector have the same size at dimension eight, two cubed: 8 = 2*2*2.
hold spinor-meets-vector-at-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2
      code 2

# Its root system is the 24-cell: twenty-four roots, the twenty-four directions, pairing into twelve lines, 24 = 2*12.
hold d-four-has-twenty-four-roots
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 12
